          "html_url": "https://github.com/python-bugzilla/python-bugzilla/commit/1bc70c4e17efa98aa64541f943e665418f0f9a29",
          "message": "rhbugzilla: Turn converter functions into a static class\n\nThis decouples the class inheritance magic and makes it more clear\nin Bugzilla() when exactly behavior is changing for rhbz handling\n\nSigned-off-by: Cole Robinson <crobinso@redhat.com>",
          "author": "Cole Robinson",
          "date": "2020-01-09T16:19:17Z"
        },
        {
          "sha": "e28881e74057099e99f41d1d06a3cc9f0d7ab3ef",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/python-bugzilla/python-bugzilla/commit/e28881e74057099e99f41d1d06a3cc9f0d7ab3ef",
          "message": "rhbugzilla: Move alias handling into BugzillaBase\n\nThe subclass hackery is kinda crazy, this is a step to unwinding it.\nTrack _is_redhat_bugzilla internally in the base class, and use that\nto determine whether to use RHBugzilla field aliases or not\n\nSigned-off-by: Cole Robinson <crobinso@redhat.com>",
          "author": "Cole Robinson",
          "date": "2020-01-09T15:50:20Z"
        },
        {
          "sha": "0bdf89d449ddf426dc82a6b38e3a7a2b36a59397",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/python-bugzilla/python-bugzilla/commit/0bdf89d449ddf426dc82a6b38e3a7a2b36a59397",
          "message": "rhbugzilla: Move external_bug API wrappers to BugzillaBase\n\nWhile RHBugzilla is the only instance that I know of with this\nextension enabled, it's not strictly rhbugzilla specific behavior,\nand keeping it separate framents the API. Move it\n\nSigned-off-by: Cole Robinson <crobinso@redhat.com>",
          "author": "Cole Robinson",
